From: Rakina Zata Amni <rakina@chromium.org>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 17:37:30 -0700
Subject: Validate opaque origins on synchronous about:blank commits

Before the first navigation in a frame, the browser sets the last
committed origin in SetOriginDependentStateOfNewFrame(). For synchronous
about:blank commits, the origin reported by the renderer in
DidCommitProvisionalLoadParams should agree with this browser-derived
value.

The existing check in DidCommitNavigationInternal() only covered the
case where the renderer reports a non-opaque origin, and when the
browser-derived origin was opaque it passed an empty GURL to
Origin::CanBeDerivedFrom(), which DCHECKs on invalid URLs. It also
accepted any opaque origin from the renderer, allowing the
browser-derived origin to be silently replaced.

This change branches on whether the browser-derived origin is opaque.
When it is, the renderer-reported origin must also be opaque with a
matching precursor; the nonce is not yet compared because the browser
and renderer can still derive different nonces for popups opened from
CSP-sandboxed documents with allow-popups-to-escape-sandbox. When it is
not opaque, the existing CanBeDerivedFrom() check is applied (now always
with a valid URL), and the "became opaque" case remains allowed for the
same popup scenario.

